  (210071, '42309ac3-afc5-4a9f-8966-b9d44c81f974' , NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The inclusion criteria are as follows:

1.  Males or females ≥18 years of age who have provided written informed consent prior to completing any study-specific procedure [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, p. 16]
2.  Disease state and prior therapies: [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, p. 16]
    a.  Dose Escalation and Dose Confirmation Periods: Histologically- or cytologically-confirmed advanced/metastatic solid tumor or lymphoma by pathology report and who has received, or been intolerant to, all approved therapies. Advanced solid tumors (i.e. including but not limited to melanoma, breast, head and neck squamous cell) and lymphomas (i.e. including by not limited to diffuse large B cell lymphoma) of any type are eligible for enrollment. [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, p. 16]
    b.  Dose Expansion Period: Histologically or cytologically confirmed diagnosis of: epithelial cancer of the ovary, fallopian tube, or peritoneum which is platinum resistant or platinum refractory. Patients must have received at least 2 prior lines of therapy. Patients with known BRCA mutation positive must have been treated with and progressed on at least 1 prior PARPi (poly(ADP-ribose) polymerase inhibitor). [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, p. 17]
3.  No limit to the number of prior therapies [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, p. 17]
    a.  Patients who refuse standard treatments may also be considered provided that he/she has been made aware of all therapeutic options and it is documented in the study records. [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, p. 17]
4.  Lesions for intratumoral injection and biopsies: [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, p. 17]
    a.  Dose Escalation: A minimum of one non-visceral lesion that is easily accessible for injection where easily accessible is defined as a cutaneous or subcutaneous mass that is palpable and/or visualizable by ultrasound [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, p. 17]
    b.  Dose Confirmation: A minimum of one visceral lesion injectable with ultrasound or computer tomography (CT) guidance and that is not encasing or abutting major vascular structures or are in a location that are considered high risk for AEs by the enrolling physician [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, p. 17]
    c.  Dose Expansion: A minimum of one lesion amenable to injection (either non-visceral or visceral). Patients must have a tumor lesion amenable to biopsy and consent to a pre-treatment and an on-treatment biopsy. For patients with only one lesion amenable to injection, biopsy, and RECIST assessment, the lesion must be ≥ 2 cm. [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, p. 17]
    d.  Biopsy Cohort Enrichment: Patients must have a tumor lesion amenable to biopsy and consent to a pre-treatment and an on-treatment biopsy [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, p. 17]
5.  All lesion(s) targeted for the initial injection must be ≥ 0.5 cm on longest diameter, be at least 5 mm thick, and have distinct borders based on exam or imaging, not close to critical structures such as major vessels, nerves, or airways [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, p. 17]
6.  Patients must have measurable disease as determined by RECIST v1.1 (solid tumors) or Cheson 2014 criteria (lymphomas). [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, p. 17]
    a.  Dose Expansion: Patients must have at least 1 measurable lesion per RECIST v1.1 which has not been previously irradiated. [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, p. 17]
7.  Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) performance status of ≤1 [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, p. 17]
8.  Adequate laboratory values: [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, pp. 17-18]
    Bone marrow function [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, pp. 17-18]
    a.  Absolute neutrophil count ≥1.5 × 10^9/L [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, pp. 17-18]
    b.  Hemoglobin ≥9 g/dL or ≥6.2 mmol/L [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, pp. 17-18]
    c.  Platelets ≥100 × 10^9/L without transfusion support [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, pp. 17-18]
    Hepatic function [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, pp. 17-18]
    d.  Aspartate aminotransferase and alanine aminotransferase ≤2.5 × upper limit of normal (ULN) (≤5 × ULN, if hepatic involvement of tumor) [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, pp. 17-18]
    e.  Bilirubin ≤1.5 × ULN (<3.0 mg/dL if patient has Gilbert’s disease) [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, pp. 17-18]
    Renal function [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, pp. 17-18]
    f.  Serum creatinine ≤1.5 × ULN or creatinine clearance of >50 mL/min (using Cockcroft-Gault formula) [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, pp. 17-18]
    Coagulation function [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, pp. 17-18]
    g.  Protime/international normalized ratio and activated partial thromboplastin time ≤1.5 × ULN [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, pp. 17-18]
    Thyroid function [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, pp. 17-18]
    h.  Thyroid-stimulating hormone within normal range [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, pp. 17-18]
9.  Female patients of childbearing potential must have a negative serum pregnancy test during screening. Male and female patients must agree to use a highly reliable method of birth control (expected failure rate less than 1% per year) from the Screening visit through 120 days after the last dose of study drug. Patients must consent to following the contraception requirements in Section 10.14.1 and 10.14.2 [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, pp. 17-18]
10. Must have a life expectancy of at least 12 weeks [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, pp. 17-18]
11. Body weight >30 kg. [Source: Prot_000 Moderna.pdf, pp. 17-18]' , 'unknown' , NULL, NULL, '2026-02-09 20:19:52'),
