*   "Neurologic or neuromuscular conditions other than SMA." [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, pp. 51-52]
*   "Anemia (Hgb < 9.5 gm/dl ; <5.9 mmol/L), leukopenia (CTCAE" [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, pp. 51-52]
*   "Hepatic dysfunction (AST or ALT CTCAE Grade 1 or higher, ≥" [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, pp. 51-52]
*   "Age adjusted renal dysfunction with eGFR calculated using the" [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, pp. 51-52]
*   "≤ 26 mL/min/1.73 m2 up to age 28 days of age" [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, pp. 51-52]
*   "≤ 30 mL/min/1.73 m2 for 1 to 3 months of age" [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, pp. 51-52]
*   "≤ 40 mL/min/1.73 m2 for 3 to 6 months of age" [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, pp. 51-52]
*   "≤ 50 mL/min/1.73 m2 for 6 to 12 months of age" [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, pp. 51-52]
*   "Clinically significant abnormalities in hematology or clinical" [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, pp. 51-52]
*   "Intractable seizure disorder (other than inactive febrile seizures)." [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, pp. 52-53]
*   "Persistent (in the opinion of the Investigator) hypoxemia (O2" [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, pp. 52-53]
*   "Presence of an untreated or inadequately treated active infection" [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, pp. 52-53]
*   "Current diagnosis of cardiac and/or vascular abnormalities" [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, pp. 52-53]
*   "Prohibited Concomitant Medications used to treat SMA, including" [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, pp. 52-53]
*   "Excluding SMA, any medically unstable condition including" [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, pp. 52-53]
*   "Acute or ongoing medical condition that, according to the Site" [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, pp. 52-53]
*   "Use of gene transfer at any time or other investigational drugs" [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, pp. 52-53]
