− Patients should be thoroughly evaluated to rule out any
alternative  etiology  (eg,  disease  progression  or
infections).
− Steroids should be considered in the absence of clear
alternative etiology even for low-grade events (Grade 2),
in order to prevent potential progression to higher grade
event.
