  (151007, 360001, 'building:an-open-label-mu-r6xt5' , 214, 'dosing' , '5.4.1 Dose escalation guidelines' , 97, 97, 216, '6670628cf8752d40413639d1de1cf933f285043c0e9927bc77c4d0caccd50555' , 'Section: 5.4.1 Dose escalation guidelines (dosing, p.97)

The MTD is the highest drug dosage that is unlikely (<25% posterior probability) to cause DLT
in more than 25% of the treated patients in the first 2 weeks of the LMI070 treatment.
A two-parameter Bayesian logistic regression model (BLRM) employing the escalation with
overdose control (EWOC) principle (Neuenschwander et al 2008; Babb et al 1998) will be used
during the dose escalation to guide dose level selection and to estimate the MTD.
Dose escalation will continue until the MTD is reached or until Novartis and Investigators reach
consensus that, based on a review of the totality of the clinical data (e.g., DLT, lower grade AE,
PK, PD, etc.) there is no benefit to continue escalation.
Estimation of the MTD during the escalation part of the study will be based upon the estimation
of the probability of DLT in the first 2 weeks in patients in the Dose-Determining Set (DDS).
The corresponding statistical methodology is described in Section 11.4.2.' , '[object Object]' , '2026-02-10 15:23:00', '2026-02-10 15:23:00'),
