 Every PK assessment includes two blood draws: one blood draw just before dosing the
patient, and another one 4 hours after dosing, except for a single PK blood draw at EoS.
 For any clinically significant increase in cardiac enzymes (Troponin / NTproBNP), repeat
test within 1 week, if enzymes remain elevated, obtain pediatric cardiology consult,
perform unscheduled echocardiogram and ECG if not already done for the visit.
