Administration of Blood product
Convalescent plasma (2 units of approximately 250mL) will be administered within 12 hours after
randomization, with a second administration (2 units of approximately 250mL) 24 to 36 hours after the
first administration.
In the situation of non-feasibility to transfuse the plasma units overnight, the two first plasma units will be
administered at the latest the next morning after randomization
Plasma should not be transfused with the usal speed of 30 to 45 minutes but should be administered at a
maximal speed of 50-100 millilitres per hour. This will reduce the risk of volume overload significantly.
