  (180084, 390001, 'building:a-randomized-ope-fi7ee' , 83, 'general' , '8.2.2.1 General Approach' , 32, 33, 425, '8e1dcffb3b29f8f5402a2bb6f72516b881bf2d2a44f081a13629f67f19db7b8a' , 'Section: 8.2.2.1 General Approach (general, pp.32-33)

This is an open label controlled randomized trial testing a superiority hypothesis with a two-sided type I
error rate of 0.05. In this explorarory study, secondary hypotheses will be tested in a non-hierachical way
and without adjustment to the significance level for multiple testing. Hence, care should be taken with
the interpretation of the significant results, since the probability of a false-positive result for any of the
secondary endpoints will be considerably higher than 5%.
Due to the dynamic and changing nature of the disease, patient population and Standard of Care, time
will be accounted for by adjusting all analyses for a period factor. At the Blind Review Meeting (see
section 8.2.1 – Per Protocol Set), the periods will be defined and finalized in a blinded manner.
All data will be summarized using appropriate summary statistics by treatment group. Continuous data
will be described by their mean value and standard deviation, or median and interquartile range if serious
deviations from the normal distribution are observed. Categorical data will be summarized by observed
counts and percentages. Time-to-event data will be summarized by event rates, obtained using Kaplan-
Meier methodology or Cumulative Incidence Functions (CIF) when competing risks are present.
