6. Taking into account the nature of the processing, the Data Processor shall assist the Data
Controller, by means of appropriate technical and organizational measures, insofar as this is
possible, in fulfilling its obligation to respond to requests from Data Participants pursuant to laws
and regulations in the area of privacy and data protection (such as, the right of access, the right to
rectification, the right to erasure, the right to restrict the processing, the right to data portability
and the right to object)
7. The Data Processor shall upon request provide the Data Controller with sufficient information to
enable the Data Controller to ensure that the Data Processor\'s obligations under this DPA are
complied with, including ensuring that the appropriate technical and organizational security
measures have been implemented.
