2. The End of Treatment Visit is conducted when the investigator determines that study drug(s) will no longer be used. If routine laboratory tests (eg,
hematology, serum chemistry) are completed within 7 days before the End of Treatment Visit, tests need not be repeated. Tumor assessment is not required
at the End of Treatment Visit provided that fewer than 6 weeks have passed since the last assessment.
3. The Safety Follow-up Visit is required to be conducted 30 days (± 7 days) after the last dose of study drug(s), or before the initiation of a new anticancer
treatment, whichever occurs first.' , '[object Object]' , '2026-02-11 05:53:48', '2026-02-11 05:53:48'),
