While some nontarget lesions may actually be measurable, they need not be measured and
instead should be assessed only qualitatively at the timepoints specified in the protocol.
• CR: Disappearance of all nontarget lesions and normalization of tumor marker level.
All lymph nodes must be nonpathological in size (< 10 mm short axis).
• PD: Unequivocal progression (as detailed below) of existing nontarget lesions. (Note:
The appearance of 1 or more new lesions is also considered progression.)
