disease individual patients might be escalated from lower to higher dose.
In Part 3 patients will continue receiving doses that they have been receiving at time of transition
into Part 3. If, in the opinion of the investigator a patient receiving 0.625 mg/kg experiences no
further clinical improvement of the condition or even disease progression, the dose may be
increased to 2.5 mg/kg. Similarly, if the investigator has any safety concerns for a patient
receiving 2.5 mg/kg, the dose may be decreased to 0.625 mg/kg after consultation with the
Sponsor.
