Gastrointestinal Effects
In this ongoing study in Type 1 SMA patients the majority of gastrointestinal events were Grade
1 and 2, were not related to study drug and resolved while on treatment.
In the healthy volunteer study in healthy adult participants 7 out of 8 participants in this Cohort
4 (420 mg branaplam) reported diarrhea (5 branaplam and 2 placebo-treated) on Day 1 with a
spontaneous recovery by Day 2.
