  (300800, 510003, 'building:an-open-label-mu-z4wyc' , 364, 'eligibility' , 'Eligibility criteria (structured)' , 87, 95, 1780, '4e4aa2e72bc699c5af6201bd7f8a23428b0fac9e4f734148eb1ddeb07970f322' , 'Structured Eligibility Criteria

Inclusion Criteria:
- 6. Must have or agree to have placement of feeding tube for enteral access via nasogastric (NG), nasojejunal (NJ), percutaneous gastrostomy (PEG), or percutaneous jejunostomy (PEJ) tube for dosing LMI070 (Part 1 only and for patients who cannot be administered orally; tube may be removed between doses) (x) X
- 7. Medical care meets and is expected to continue to meet guidelines set out in the Consensus Statement for Standard of Care in SMA (Wang et al 2007), in the opinion of the Site Investigator. (x) 8. At birth gestational age >32 weeks and body weight at birth >2 kg. (x) X
- 9. Must live within 2 hours drive of study center. Clearance should be obtained from the site investigator and sponsor if the patient resides more than 2 hours ground travel from the study center. (x) X
- 10. Able to complete all study procedures, measurements and visits; and parent or guardian/patient has adequately supportive psychosocial circumstances, in the opinion of the Site Investigator. Screening: Baseline: Criteria (x) 1. Written informed consent must be obtained from the parent / guardian before any assessment is performed. (x) 2. Type 1 SMA, diagnosed with genetic confirmation of mutations in both alleles of the SMN1 gene, and with SMN2 copy number of 2. (x) 3. Best supportive care in place and stable for at least 14 days before screening as assessed by the investigator. (x) 4. Age at screening up to 180 days of age (x) X 5. Must be able to demonstrate antigravity strength in both biceps. (x) X

Exclusion Criteria:
- 3. Anemia (Hgb < 9.5 gm/dl ; <5.9 mmol/L), leukopenia (CTCAE Grade 2 or higher, <3000 /mm3; <3.0 x109/L), neutropenia (Grade 2 or higher, <1,500/mm3; < 1.5 X 109/L) or thrombocytopenia (CTCAE Grade 2 or higher, ≤ 75,000/mm3), ≤75 X 109/L X
- 4. Hepatic dysfunction (e.g. AST or ALT CTCAE Grade 1 or higher, ≥ ULN if considered to be consequence of hepatic dysfunction); total bilirubin CTCAE Grade 1 or higher, ≥ ULN). Novartis Confidential Page 90 Amended Protocol Version 11 (clean) Protocol No. CLMI070X2201 Screening: Baseline: Criteria X
- 5. Age adjusted renal dysfunction with eGFR calculated using the following formula: eGFR (in mL/min/1.73 m2) = 0.45 X Length (cm) ÷ serum creatinine (mg/dl) (Schwartz and Work 2009). ≤ 26 mL/min/1.73 m2 up to age 28 days of age ≤ 30 mL/min/1.73 m2 for 1 to 3 months of age ≤ 40 mL/min/1.73 m2 for 3 to 6 months of age ≤ 50 mL/min/1.73 m2 for 6 to 12 months of age X
- 6. Clinically significant abnormalities in hematology or clinical chemistry parameters, as assessed by the investigator, at screening that would render the patient unsuitable for inclusion (x) 7. Intractable seizure disorder (other than inactive febrile seizures). (x) X
- 8. Persistent (in the opinion of the investigator) hypoxemia (O2 saturation awake <92% or O2 saturation asleep <91%, without ventilation support) or requiring oral suctioning >2 per day (x) X 9. Presence of an untreated or inadequately treated active infection requiring systemic antiviral or antimicrobial therapy at any time during the screening period. (x) X
- 10. Current diagnosis of cardiac and/or vascular abnormalities including uncontrolled hypertension, intolerance of blood pressure and pulse assessment techniques such that consistent normal values cannot be measured, echocardiographic abnormalities (both structural and function) or ECG abnormalities (such as long QT, heart block or Torsade’s) indicating significant risk of safety for infant patients participating in the study such as: Concomitant clinically significant pediatric cardiac arrhythmias, e.g. sustained ventricular tachycardia, and clinically significant second or third degree AV block. (x) X
- 11. Prohibited Concomitant Medications used to treat SMA, including but not exclusively: oral albuterol or oral salbutamol, hydroxurea, riluzole, valproate, carnitine, creatine, sodium phenylbutyrate within 14 days prior to enrollment or during the study. X
- 12. Excluding SMA, any medically unstable condition including cardiomyopathy, hepatic dysfunction, kidney disorder, endocrine disorder, GI disorders, prematurity of <32 weeks gestation, metabolic disorders, severe respiratory compromise and significant brain abnormalities or injuries including hypoxic-ischemic encephalopathy. X
- 13. Acute or ongoing medical condition that, according to the Site Investigator and discussed with sponsor, would interfere with the conduct and assessments of the study. Examples are medical disability other than SMA that would interfere with the assessment of safety or would compromise the ability of the patient to undergo study procedures including be assessed by CHOP INTEND infant motor scale, changes in hematologic parameters or gastrointestinal dysfunction that would compromise the ability of adequate assessment of safety Novartis Confidential Page 91 Amended Protocol Version 11 (clean) Protocol No. CLMI070X2201 Screening: Baseline: Criteria (x) Use of gene transfer at any time or other investigational drugs within 14 days. (x) Patients who have received nusinersen at any time prior to screening (x) Neurologic or neuromuscular conditions other than SMA. X Anemia ( CTCAE Grade 2 or higher Hgb < 10 gm/dl ; <6.2 mmol/L ),Leukopenia (CTCAE Grade 2 or higher, <3000 /mm3; <3.0 x109/L), neutropenia (Grade 2 or higher, <1,500/mm3; < 1.5 X 109/L) or thrombocytopenia (CTCAE Grade 2 or higher, ≤ 75,000/mm3), ≤75 X 109/L X Hepatic dysfunction (e.g. AST or ALT CTCAE Grade 1 or higher, ≥ ULN, if considered to be consequence of hepatic dysfunction); total bilirubin CTCAE Grade 1 or higher, ≥ ULN). X Age adjusted renal dysfunction with eGFR calculated using the following formula: eGFR (in mL/min/1.73 m2) = 0.45 X Length (cm) ÷ serum creatinine (mg/dl) (Schwartz and Work 2009). ≤ 26 mL/min/1.73 m2 up to age 28 days of age ≤ 30 mL/min/1.73 m2 for 1 to 3 months of age ≤ 40 mL/min/1.73 m2 for 3 to 6 months of age ≤ 50 mL/min/1.73 m2 for 6 to12 months of age X Clinically significant abnormalities in hematology or clinical chemistry parameters, as assessed by the Site Investigator, at screening that would render the patient unsuitable for inclusion (x) Intractable epilepsy (x) X Persistent (in the opinion of the Investigator) hypoxemia (O2 saturation awake <92% or O2 saturation asleep <91%, without ventilation support), (x) X Presence of an untreated or inadequately treated active infection requiring systemic antiviral or antimicrobial therapy at any time during the screening period. X Current diagnosis of cardiac and/or vascular abnormalities including uncontrolled hypertension, intolerance of blood pressure and pulse assessment techniques such that consistent normal values cannot be measured, echocardiographic abnormalities (both structural and function) or ECG abnormalities (such as long QT, heart block or Torsade’s) indicating significant risk of safety for infant patients participating in the study such as: Concomitant clinically significant pediatric cardiac arrhythmias, e.g. sustained ventricular tachycardia, and clinically significant second or third degree AV block. Clinically significant findings identified by an echocardiogram performed at screening (x) X Prohibited Concomitant Medications used to treat SMA: oral albuterol or oral salbutamol, hydroxurea, riluzole, valproate, carnitine, creatine, sodium phenylbutyrate within 14 days prior to enrollment or during the study. X Excluding SMA, any medically unstable condition including cardiomyopathy, hepatic dysfunction, kidney disorder, endocrine disorder, GI disorders, metabolic disorders, severe respiratory compromise and significant brain abnormalities or injuries including hypoxic-ischemic encephalopathy. Novartis Confidential Page 92 Amended Protocol Version 11 (clean) Protocol No. CLMI070X2201 Screening: Baseline: Criteria X Acute or ongoing medical condition that, according to the Site Investigator and discussed with sponsor, would interfere with the conduct and assessments of the study. Examples are medical disability other than SMA that would interfere with the assessment of safety or would compromise the ability of the patient to undergo study procedures including be assessed by CHOP INTEND infant motor scale, changes in hematologic parameters or gastrointestinal dysfunction that would compromise the ability of adequate assessment of safety Note: In the case where a safety laboratory assessment at screening is outside of the range specified above, the assessment may be repeated once prior to dosing. If the repeat value remains outside of the specified ranges, the patient should not be dosed and may be excluded from the study after discussion between the principal investigator and the sponsor. In borderline situations, where the clinical relevance of the result is unclear, additional repetition of the assessment over a limited time frame may be considered. There are no specific exclusion criteria.' , '[object Object]' , '2026-02-11 06:06:03', '2026-02-11 06:06:03'),
