Eligible adult patients who tested positive for SARS-CoV-2 and are admitted to the hospital will be
randomized and assessed daily during hospitalization. Discharged patients will be contacted by telephone
at days 15, 30 and 90. All subjects will undergo efficacy and safety assessments, including laboratory assays,
which are aligned with clinical care. Only an extra blood sample will be drawn at baseline. Also blood
samples and nasopharyngeal swabs will be done according to clinical need (standard of care). If feasible, an
additional nasopharyngeal swab will be taken on day 6. The study should not put an extra burden on
healthcare workers and on the hospital’s resources.
