  (330084, 150001, 'sample:a-randomized-open-tlkf8' , 83, 'general' , '8.2.2.1 General Approach' , 32, 33, 425, '8e1dcffb3b29f8f5402a2bb6f72516b881bf2d2a44f081a13629f67f19db7b8a' , 'Section: 8.2.2.1 General Approach (general, pp.32-33)

This is an open label controlled randomized trial testing a superiority hypothesis with a two-sided type I
error rate of 0.05. In this explorarory study, secondary hypotheses will be tested in a non-hierachical way
and without adjustment to the significance level for multiple testing. Hence, care should be taken with
the interpretation of the significant results, since the probability of a false-positive result for any of the
secondary endpoints will be considerably higher than 5%.
Due to the dynamic and changing nature of the disease, patient population and Standard of Care, time
will be accounted for by adjusting all analyses for a period factor. At the Blind Review Meeting (see
section 8.2.1 – Per Protocol Set), the periods will be defined and finalized in a blinded manner.
All data will be summarized using appropriate summary statistics by treatment group. Continuous data
will be described by their mean value and standard deviation, or median and interquartile range if serious
deviations from the normal distribution are observed. Categorical data will be summarized by observed
counts and percentages. Time-to-event data will be summarized by event rates, obtained using Kaplan-
Meier methodology or Cumulative Incidence Functions (CIF) when competing risks are present.
-- 33 of 47 --
Protocol: DAWN-Plasma
Internal Ref.: 63992 Version: 2.5 27/10/2020
All treatment comparisons will be adjusted for study site and period, both included as fixed factors in the
model. An appropriate measure of the treatment effect (e.g. mean difference, odds ratio, hazard ratio)
will be estimated for all primary and secondary endpoints and presented along with its associated 95%
confidence interval.
A statistical analysis plan (SAP) will be developed and filed with the study sponsor prior to database lock.
Missing Clinical Status data during hospital stay and at Day 15 and 30 will be accounted for by multiple
imputation, whereby a total of 100 imputations will be done. The imputation methodology will be fully
described in the Statistical Analyis Plan.' , '[object Object]' , '2026-02-11 19:26:48', '2026-02-11 19:26:48'),
  (330085, 150001, 'sample:a-randomized-open-tlkf8' , 84, 'endpoints' , '8.2.2.2 Analysis of the Primary Efficacy Endpoint' , 33, 33, 117, 'a679f79f9016f97fa609ad73e59a7215afe0590dfbc2d33a43e230924338a8ba' , 'Section: 8.2.2.2 Analysis of the Primary Efficacy Endpoint (endpoints, p.33)

The primary endpoint is defined as the number of patients alive without mechanical ventilation at day 15
after randomization. Treatment groups will be compared using a logistic regression analysis adjusted for
study site and study period , both included as fixed factors in the model (see Section 8.2.2.1 – second
paragraph). The treatment effect will be estimated as an odds ratio from this model.
The analysis of the primary endpoint will be performed for the FAS and PPS (if defined).' , '[object Object]' , '2026-02-11 19:26:48', '2026-02-11 19:26:48'),
  (330086, 150001, 'sample:a-randomized-open-tlkf8' , 85, 'endpoints' , '8.2.2.3 Analysis of the Secondary Endpoints' , 33, 33, 317, 'fcd71e7570157aae823bbee531d45e0842517127f176acd43085829c9348a9da' , 'Section: 8.2.2.3 Analysis of the Secondary Endpoints (endpoints, p.33)

All efficacy endpoints will be assessed for both the FAS and PSS (if defined). Secondary endpoints
evaluating the safety of convalescent plasma will be assessed for the FAS only. The following statistical
methods will be used:
1. All-Cause mortality rates will be estimated by treatment group using the Kaplan-Meier method.
The resulting Kaplan-Meier curves will be compared using a log-rank test. The treatment effect
will be estimated by the hazard ratio using a Cox regression, adjusted for study site and period.
2. Time-to-event parameters with competing risk (time to clinical improvement, incidence of
supplemental oxygen, mechanical ventilation, ECMO and ICU admission): event rates will be
estimated using cumulative incidence functions (CIF), the resulting CIF curves will be compared
using Gray’s test. The treatment effect will be estimated by the subdistribution hazard ratio
using a Gray’s regression analysis, adjusted for study site and period.
3. Duration of hospital and ICU stay, supplemental oxygen, mechanical ventilation and ECMO:
these will be analysed as time-to-event parameters with competing risk, whereby the event of
interest is life discharge from hospital/ICU and the competing risk is hospital/ICU death.
4. Continuous variables (e.g. QTc, NT50, QoL) will be analysed using a general linear model
including study site and period as factors and, if applicable, the baseline value as covafxriate.
Treatment effects will be estimated by the difference in mean values between the groups. If
applicable, changes from baseline will be calculated.' , '[object Object]' , '2026-02-11 19:26:48', '2026-02-11 19:26:48'),
