Early analysis
Early analyses include monitoring enrolment, baseline characteristics, and follow-up rates throughout the
course of the study by the study team..
In case the study is terminated early either due to safety concerns or clear evidence of
efficacy/futility/safety from external studies, the following analyses will be performed for the primary
outcome:
1) A Bayesian logistic regression analysis will be performed on the primary efficacy endpoint in
order to obtain a posterior probability of a positive treatment effect. Full details will be
provided in the SAP.
2) Conditional power will be calculated for the originally planned sample size (n=483) based on data
collected up to time of termination. Full details will be provided in the SAP.
Interim analyses
No formal interim analysis will be planned. A data and safety monitoring committee (DSMB) will monitor
ongoing results to ensure patient well-being and safety as well as study integrity. The DSMB, containing
one statistician, will have the opportunity to ask for data, to require analyses or to compare Belgian trial
results with results available from other countries. The DSMB will be asked to recommend early
termination or modification only when there is clear and substantial evidence of a safety issue.' , '[object Object]' , '2026-02-11 19:26:48', '2026-02-11 19:26:48'),
