evaluated by comparing predicted
steady state PK concentrations (5th, median, and 95th percentiles) using the population PK model. A fixed
dose of 750 mg was selected to approximate 10 mg/kg (based on median body weight of ~75 kg). A total
of 1000 patients were simulated using body weight distribution of 40 to 120 kg. Simulation results
demonstrate that body weight-based and fixed dosing regimens yield similar median steady state PK
concentrations with slightly less overall between-patient variability with fixed dosing regimen.
A fixed dosing approach is preferred by the prescribing community due to ease of use and reduced dosing
errors. Given the expectation of similar PK exposure and variability, AstraZeneca considered it feasible to
switch to fixed dosing regimens for durvalumab. Based on an average body weight of 75 kg, a fixed dose
