1  17 Jun 2021  2.0  Substantial  1. Clarification of exclusion criterion for women
based on latest NICE guidance.
2. Addition of exclusion criterion for patients
already enrolled in a Clinical trial.
3. Clarification of per protocol and per treatment
analysis.
4. Addition of imaging sub-study.
5. Other minor/non-substantial corrections.
2  27 Jan 2022  3.0  Substantial  1. Option for Primary Care investigators to send
out text messages via NHS clinical systems to
potentially eligible participants.
2. Addition of mechanism for potential study
participants to contact the central study team
after invitation from Primary Care investigators.
3. Addition of new links to NICE prescribing
support for anticoagulation.
4. Update to Key Study Contacts page.
3  06 Jun 2022  4.0  Substantial  1. Revision of age inclusion criteria from 60-73
to 55-73 years based on updates received from
live national screening data.
2. Reorganisation of selection criteria to
separate the automated screening processes
from elements requiring Primary Care input.
3. Clarification that only patients with prior
systemic thromboembolism should be excluded.
4. Clarification of a 3-year time period for
exclusion of patients with prior major bleeding
that required hospitalisation.
5. Updates made to Section 9.3 to reflect
changes in data management within CPRD.
6. Other minor/non-substantial corrections,
including updates to the trial flowchart.
4  21 Jul 2022  4.1  Substantial
[additions
following MHRA
review of v4.0]
1. Additional exclusion criterion for women who
are of childbearing potential (WOCBP).
2. Addition and amendment of protocol text
relating to WOCBP.
3. WOCBP added to sub-study exclusion list
and clarification of inclusion periods.
