Eligible participants who have been successfully screened and invited by their Primary Care team will
be directed to a Research Electronic Data Capture case report system (REDCap) electronic form to
consent to communication by the central study team. After reviewing the PPI information video,
potential participants will be asked to complete the ‘consent to contact’ form by entering their name,
Primary Care practice name, telephone number, email address and best timeslot for contact. Central
study staff will then telephone the potential participant, go through any questions arising from the
Participant Information Sheet, and activate the REDCap e-consent process as documented in section
3.8.
