emailed to the participant. The participant’s NHS number is entered by the Investigator at the time of
confirming the participant’s consent on REDCap.' , '[object Object]' , '2026-02-12 17:17:21', '2026-02-12 17:17:21'),
  (390377, 570034, 'sample:preventing-strok-13m40' , 162, 'general' , '9.2 Data security at University Hospitals Birmingham (lead NHS institution)' , 51, 51, 208, '01f1f9e9fab0a5b4471f7dcb023343672bc8ce6031d5286fbddd7aebe56078cb' , 'Section: 9.2 Data security at University Hospitals Birmingham (lead NHS institution) (general, p.51)

Personal data for consented participants will be stored in a dedicated sever within the University
Hospitals Birmingham NHS Foundation Trust infrastructure and behind the Health and Social Care
Network (HSCN) firewall. This includes a copy of identifiers and patient-reported EQ-5D-5L collected
on REDCap, outcome and safety data from CPRD/HES/ONS, and cognitive function data from the
University of Oxford Online Questionnaire Sharing Service. All data and results will be backed up
within the same environment and will be allocated to isolated data containers.
All patient level data will be stored for a minimum period of 5 years as per NHS requirements. Data
access will be monitored and limited to authorised users who will be granted password restricted
audited access through Secure Shell (SSH; a cryptographic network protocol). A Data Privacy Impact
Assessment has been completed. No identifiable data will be moved, manipulated or stored outside of
this environment.' , '[object Object]' , '2026-02-12 17:17:21', '2026-02-12 17:17:21'),
  (390378, 570034, 'sample:preventing-strok-13m40' , 163, 'general' , '9.3 Data security at CPRD' , 51, 51, 376, 'b2632c3dfd043d125756d0d39757cd977b576423bb68037cf270bcc10b3d6a39' , 'Section: 9.3 Data security at CPRD (general, p.51)

The CPRD platform enables secure screening of patients for recruitment and does not require sharing
of any patient identifiers outside the practice.
The CPRD IRSP environment is self-contained, within its own set of Azure Subscriptions and
managed by NTT Data Business Solutions (UK) Ltd. Access to the server infrastructure is managed
using an Azure Bastion, which is only available through the Microsoft Azure Portal, and limited to
MHRA, NTT Data and specific IP address ranges. CPRD IRSP servers are hosted on Azure in
Microsoft’s UK South Cloud-Hosted Data Centre. No non-Microsoft employees can gain access to the
data centres. Any vendor that is allowed to access the data centre follows very stringent protocols for
any access they are granted
The CPRD network is segmented into two parts; an internal subnet that contains the machines in the
irsp.cprd.com Windows domain, and a demilitarized zone which contains the standalone internet-
facing servers (e.g. webservers). There is also a link to CPRD infrastructure. Strict firewall policies
control the flow of traffic between the various zones, to control potential lateral movement on the part
of an attacker, and to prevent unnecessary exposure of services.
User access to the IRSP environment is managed by the CPRD Interventional Research team.
Access is granted based on the user’s role (either within the Team, or as Study Investigators or patient
end-users). IRSP uses a two-factor authentication for external users (Investigators and Patients) and a
Single Sign On for internal users (MHRA staff) using their MHRA account and password.
CPRD SOPs and policies are in place that define the policies and procedures for data access and
external data transfer. A full list is defined in the trial Data Management Plan.' , '[object Object]' , '2026-02-12 17:17:21', '2026-02-12 17:17:21'),
  (390379, 570034, 'sample:preventing-strok-13m40' , 164, 'general' , '9.4 Data security for cognitive function' , 51, 52, 213, '180d334c28483fea46edabb3d5f5ab992ee2d849fd65b5b0aa78550fb6bc5958' , 'Section: 9.4 Data security for cognitive function (general, pp.51-52)

Data is collected by a dedicated Linux server protected by the main watchguard firewall at the Nuffield
Department of Population Health (NDPH; University of Oxford). Information collected is stored within
