9.1. Pharmacodynamics
9.1.1. Hemodynamics
Pulmonary arterial catheters will be placed in all participants enrolled. Participants will
consent to have the catheter inserted for the purposes of the study. Catheter placement
may be confirmed by chest X-ray or fluoroscopy, as clinically indicated. All effort will
be made to minimize radiation exposure time.
Variables that will be recorded from the right heart catheterization, as data permit,
include:
 right atrial pressure
 pulmonary artery systolic and diastolic pressure
 mean pulmonary artery pressure
 pulmonary wedge pressure
 cardiac output and index measured by thermodilution
