5.  Study termination. The sponsor, IRB, or regulatory agency terminates the study.
6.  Lack of efficacy. The investigator or subinvestigator has determined that the subject is not
benefiting from study treatment; and, continued participation would pose an unacceptable
risk to the subject. For example, discontinuation should be considered in the following case;
on consecutive visits, an office sitting systolic blood pressure is persistently higher by at least
