e time every day throughout the study (acceptable
range is ± 3hours) except the visit day. In case of a missed dose, the subject should take only one
dose of the study drug for the day; instructions should be provided to parents or legal guardians
that the daily dose should not be doubled on account of the missed dose. On the day before a
scheduled visit, subject must take the study drug 24 hours (acceptable range, 21 to 27 hours)
before office blood pressure measurement on the following day.
Except for Week 16, subjects will visit the study site on each visit day without taking the study
drugs, and receive them only after completing all tests, observations, and evaluations.
On the visit of Week 16, subjects, the subjects’ parent or the subjects’ legal guardian will be
instructed to visit the study site after taking the study drug and the tests, observations, and
evaluations 2 hour (acceptable time window, 1 to 3 hours) after taking the study drug will be
performed.
The investigator or subinvestigator will confirm whether the subject has taken the study drug or
not in the morning of each visit.
