Blood samples (one 1-mL sample per scheduled time) for pharmacokinetic analysis of TAK-536
will be collected into vacutainers containing ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid dipotassium salt
dihydrate (EDTA-2K). After mixing the vacutainers 5 to 6 times by inversion immediately,
vacutainers will be centrifuged at 4°C and 3000 rpm for 10 minutes. The plasma will be
dispensed from the vacutainers to polypropylene tube and be stored frozen below -20°C in a
freezer until being shipped to the analytical institute.
For each sample, the date and time of the latest study drug administration and the actual time of
blood sample collection will be recorded in the eCRF.' , '[object Object]' , '2026-02-12 18:53:12', '2026-02-12 18:53:12'),
