  (391123, 570037, 'sample:a-phase-3-open-l-rhrr4' , 152, 'safety' , '10.1.6  Causality of AEs' , 53, 53, 146, '249db43cc9780c76132b308b68d410c131d67cc20354b1bf6089e6b5d6395aee' , 'Section: 10.1.6  Causality of AEs (safety, p.53)

The relationship of each AE to study drugs will be assessed using the following categories:
Related:  An AE that follows a reasonable temporal sequence from administration of a drug (including
the course after withdrawal of the drug), or for which possible involvement of the drug cannot
be ruled out, although factors other than the drug, such as underlying diseases, complications,
concomitant medications and concurrent treatments, may also be responsible.
Not Related:  An AE that does not follow a reasonable temporal sequence from administration of a drug
and/or that can reasonably be explained by other factors, such as underlying diseases,
complications, concomitant medications and concurrent treatments.' , '[object Object]' , '2026-02-12 18:53:12', '2026-02-12 18:53:12'),
  (391124, 570037, 'sample:a-phase-3-open-l-rhrr4' , 153, 'general' , '10.1.7  Causality to Study Procedures' , 53, 53, 69, '0cfd0a90496d2a39f9d6cffc46dcee1c97626c21648c117222aafceb067a59fb' , 'Section: 10.1.7  Causality to Study Procedures (general, p.53)

Relationship (causality) to study procedures should be determined for all AEs.
The relationship should be assessed as Related if the investigator considers that there is
reasonable possibility that an event is due to a study procedure. Otherwise, the relationship
should be assessed as Not Related.' , '[object Object]' , '2026-02-12 18:53:12', '2026-02-12 18:53:12'),
  (391125, 570037, 'sample:a-phase-3-open-l-rhrr4' , 154, 'general' , '10.1.8  Start Date' , 53, 53, 36, '0b0794f8fa3b0c81168a4e636f81c2dffd59bbfa7a695a42af19d57b294800be' , 'Section: 10.1.8  Start Date (general, p.53)

