Patients who experience study treatment-related toxicity that leads to a dose interruption, following
recovery to at least Grade 1 or to baseline, continue to receive injections at 50% of the planned dose based
on investigator discretion. Patients may not be rechallenged at the planned dose.
Patients with a lesion that has become inaccessible or has decreased in tumor volume during the study
treatment period, such that the planned dose is no longer able to be administered, may continue with study
therapy at a lower dose following documented approval from Moderna.
