(pretreatment) on or after the date of first dose of study drug and up to 30 days following study
drug discontinuation (Safety Follow-up visit) or initiation of new anticancer therapy, whichever
comes first. The TEAE classification also applies to imAEs that are recorded up to 90 days after
the last dose of tislelizumab or placebo, regardless of whether or not the patient starts a new
anticancer therapy. Only those AEs that were treatment emergent will be included in summary
tables. All AEs, treatment-emergent or otherwise, will be presented in patient data listings.
