  ('e1e59797-6a3a-45e1-96ce-62ea443e9d35' , 'ai_response_generated' , '2026-02-10 15:58:26', '1' , '6502ade4-ecd4-46af-8a0b-93d5fabddfe4' , 'response' , NULL, 'generated' , '[object Object]' , NULL, 1, 'The inclusion criteria for the study are provided for Part 1 and Part 3.

**Inclusion criteria Part 1:**
1.  "Written informed consent must be obtained from the parent / guardian" [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, p. 50]
2.  "Type 1 SMA, diagnosed clinically, with symptom onset <6 months" [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, p. 50]
3.  "Best supportive care in place and stable for at least 14 days before dosing branaplam (required for the first administration only, and subsequently only for patients who cannot be dosed orally; tube may be removed between doses)." [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, p. 51]
4.  "Minimum CHOP INTEND score of 15 at baseline" [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, p. 51]
5.  "Must be able to swallow solid and liquid even if tube feeding is used to support nutrition intake and must be the 5th percentile for length or weight on the international growth curves and must be proportional in height and weight" [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, p. 51]
6.  "At birth gestational age >32 weeks and body weight at birth >2 kg" [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, p. 51]
7.  "Able to complete all study procedures, measurements and visits; and parent or guardian/patient has adequately supportive psychosocial circumstances, in the opinion of the Site Investigator." [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, p. 51]

**Inclusion criteria Part 3:**
1.  "Written informed consent must be obtained from the parent / guardian" [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, p. 51]
2.  "Current participation in Part 1 or Part 2 of the study protocol and completion of at least 52 weeks of treatment with branaplam" [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, p. 51]
3.  "Further treatment with branaplam is in the best interest of the patient as assessed by the Site Investigator" [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, p. 51]
4.  "Able to complete all study procedures, measurements and visits; and parent or guardian/patient has adequately supportive psychosocial circumstances, in the opinion of the Site Investigator" [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, p. 51]
5.  "Except for previous participation in Part 1 or Part 2 of the study and completion at least 52 weeks of treatment, no further eligibility criteria will be implemented for Part 3." [Source: Prot_000Novartis.pdf, p. 87]

